    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="1335" n="1311" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg1311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">750G.00/3–1350: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Allen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-03-13T14:00:00+01:00">March 13, 1950—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>324. I have come reluctantly to conclusion that no useful purpose can be served
                    by further consideration Trieste question at this time. In view of Italian
                    insistence on substantial implementation of tripartite declaration (Rome’s 1011,
                    March 10)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d596-f1"/> and Yugoslav reluctance to surrender
                    any Zone B territory, further Italo-Yugoslav talks would probably produce only
                    increased friction without positive accomplishments.</p>
                <p>I am inclined to believe that even now Italians can get small part Zone B,
                    including Capodistria, if they are willing to settle for that, but do not see
                    any possibility persuading Yugoslav Government to do more.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 324, repeated Rome 31, Paris 51, London 44, Trieste 17.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Allen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
